  greetings:
  - Oh! You startled me. The kids are asleep, please keep your voice down.
  - Detective. Come in, quietly.
  aboutSelf: Four kids, and a husband who works nights at the grain elevator in Barlow. I don't sleep much.
  aboutTown: It's a good place to raise children. Mostly.
  seenAnythingStrange: My youngest keeps drawing a fifth person in our family pictures. When I ask who it is, she says, 'the new one.'
  foundersDay: It poured! The kids loved it. Mae won the pie contest, cherry. She always does.
  gossip:
  - title: About Otis Pruitt
    response: Otis has six fingers on his left hand. My kids think it's the best thing in the world.
  - title: About Amos Calder
    response: Amos has started buying women's shoes at the store. Otis told me. Ruth's size.
